-- title:
--   Igusa: k(X₁(M))_q/k(X₀(M))_q is Galois in characteristic ℓ∤ M
-- statement:
--   Let $\ell$ be a prime, let $M\ge 1$ be an integer with $\ell\nmid M$, and let $k$ be a field of characteristic $\ell$. Inside the Laurent series field $k((q))$ consider two intermediate fields over $k$: $F_1$, assumed equal to [`ModularCurve.qExpFunctionFieldC k (CongruenceSubgroup.Gamma1 M)`](def/ModularCurve_X1.html#L101), and $F_0$, assumed equal to [`ModularCurve.qExpFunctionFieldC k (CongruenceSubgroup.Gamma0 M)`](def/ModularCurve_X1.html#L101); here, for a subgroup $\Gamma\le \mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z})$, `qExpFunctionFieldC k Γ` is the subfield of $k((q))$ generated over $k$ by the set of quotients $\mathrm{intSeriesC}\,k\,p_f/\mathrm{intSeriesC}\,k\,p_g$, where $f,g$ run over modular forms of a common weight $k$ on the image of $\Gamma$ in $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{R})$, $p_f,p_g$ are integral power series with `IsIntegralQExp` recording that they are the integral $q$-expansions of $f$ and $g$, and the reduction $\mathrm{intSeriesC}\,k\,p_g$ is nonzero. Assume $F_0\le F_1$. The conclusion asserts the existence of a finite group $G$ together with an action of $G$ on $F_1$ by ring automorphisms over $k$ such that: the action is faithful; every $g\in G$ fixes every element of $F_1$ that lies in $F_0$; every element of $F_1$ fixed by all of $G$ lies in $F_0$; and the cardinality of $G$ equals the index of the subgroup of $(\mathbb{Z}/M)^\times$ generated by $-1$.
--
--   This is the characteristic-$\ell$ form of Igusa's theorem on the reduction of $X_1(M)\to X_0(M)$ at a prime $\ell\nmid M$: the extension of $q$-expansion function fields stays Galois with the full diamond group $(\mathbb{Z}/M)^\times/\{\pm1\}$, hence in particular separable of that degree by Artin's criterion. It is used in the analysis of residue fields and separability at the valuation subring attached to $X_1(M)\to X_0(M)$ in characteristic $\ell$.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_exists_mulSemiringAction_faithful_fixed_iff_card_eq_index_qExpFunctionFieldC_gamma1_gamma0_charP.lean

